# Port1900 - An async Python client library for the Nex protocol

It's that time again. Time to add another small web protocol{a} to Rogallo{b}. This time it's one I stumbled across a few days ago: the Nex protocol{c}. This one is very simple and straightforward and it seemed like a shame *not* to support it.

=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/smolweb/ {a} small web protocol
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ {b} Rogallo
=> https://nightfall.city/nex/info/specification.txt {c} Nex protocol

So, as I have with Gemini{a}, Spartan{b}, Gopher{c} and Finger{d}, I've added a dedicated library for dealing with the associated URI, and to provide a client for talking to the server.

=> https://wasat.davep.dev/ {a} Gemini
=> https://sybaritic.davep.dev/ {b} Spartan
=> https://port70.davep.dev/ {c} Gopher
=> https://port79.davep.dev/ {d} Finger

The documentation can be found on the dedicated site{a}.

=> https://port1900.davep.dev/ {a} the dedicated site

